-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- H₂⁺ as expressions
-- The recurrences in the variable m = 1/n (radial) and m = 1/l (angular): each step one expression,
-- the same at every index, so one interval over m ∈ [0, 1/(N+1)] covers every step past the start.
-- radial (inputs 0 t = r_{n+1}, 1 p, 2 σ, 3 c, 4 m = 1/n): Jaffé's r_n = (n−1−σ)²/(2n² + (4p−2σ)n + c − (n+1)² t)
-- divided through by n², as 1/(1 + E/u²) with u = 1 − (1+σ)m and
-- E = m(4p + (c − 1 − (1+σ)²) m) + (1+m)²(1 − t), the excess of the denominator over the numerator
rad-u : IE
rad-u = ie-sub (ie-int 1) (ie-mul (ie-add (ie-int 1) (ie-var 2)) (ie-var 4))
